DDD2Self is based on self-supervised learning, where the model learns to remove noise directly from noisy images without needing clean ground-truth targets. The main idea of the method is a **Dynamic Data-driven Dropout (DDD)** mechanism, which adaptively changes dropout behavior during training according to image characteristics. Instead of using a fixed masking or dropout strategy, the method dynamically selects and suppresses image regions to encourage the network to learn meaningful image structures rather than simply memorizing noisy pixels. This adaptive learning process improves denoising quality, robustness, and generalization, especially in limited-data and domain-specific imaging scenarios.

